                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I am a boomer and have gaming for some 45 years now, if you count the time I spent at Aladdin's Castle in the mall in the early 80's.  Until last week, I had never experienced VR.  I got my Steam Frame last week, took a week off from work, and tried it out playing Half-Life: Alyx.\n\nI am completely blown away. Absolutely breathtaking. Took a little getting used to the controls and video after over 30 years of mouse/keyboard playing on a monitor, but I quickly adapted.\n\nAfter all of these years of sniping, bushwhacking, raiding, and blasting a veritable infinite number and type of creatures and aliens, I never realized just how bad my aim is. I have never wasted so much ammo. Shooting high, low, left, right, and \"Where the hell did that go?\"! I am getting better and I really like that there seems to be no \"hit-box\" targeting and the bullets do go where the gun is pointing, regardless of where I think I'm aiming.\n\nAs far as reloading guns! I'm so used to just tapping \"R\" mid \"run and gun\" and only have a brief interrupt to my barrage of lead. Now the hair raises on the back of my neck when I hear the \"clink\" of the empty chamber in my pistol.  I know that If I slip up and get out of sequence reloading, I'm pretty much dead.\n\nI highly recommend this game.  To me this game is a benchmark for all other VR games.  I am very fortunate that this is the game that introduced me to VR.  Thank you Steam for including it with the Steam Frame.  It definitely shows how good the Frame capabilities are.",
